maya: Hey docs team — spotted broken link in Function calling > JSON schema examples page. The SDK snippet link points to the old repo and a few examples use `required: true` inconsistently. Anyone available to fix and add a compact shim example? /cc @ashley :wave:

ashley: I can take the shim example. Can you paste the broken URL so I can reference it?

maya: Here it is: https://docs.redwood.ai/function-calling/jsonschema#examples - the SDK snippet anchor goes to an old file. Also would be great to add a compact union/array shim and a tiny fallback parsing snippet.

jonah: I can open a quick PR to update the link + replace the snippet. I'll add a JS compact shim like below and a short Python variant.

jonah: ```js
// compact shim: try parse, else fallback to lax parser
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(resp.text);
  return parsed;
} catch (e) {
  // fallback: strip trailing commas and try again
  const cleaned = resp.text.replace(/,\s*}/g, '}').replace(/,\s*]/g, ']');
  return JSON.parse(cleaned);
}
```

ashley: For Python I'll add:

ashley: ```py
# minimal fallback for union arrays
try:
    out = json.loads(text)
except ValueError:
    out = json.loads(re.sub(r',\s*}', '}', text))
```

jonah: opened PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/432 — updates link, swaps in new SDK snippet, and adds a short note: "Prefer examples that avoid required=true for optional union members." Will ping for reviews.

maya: Awesome. Can you also add a one-liner in the examples section about validators that are strict in older SDKs?

jonah: Yup, added a line and a tiny compatibility note. Ran docs build locally, all good.

deploy-bot: docs-staging build succeeded — https://staging.docs.redwood.ai/changes/1748504321 :rocket:

ashley: Reviewed and left one tiny wording nudge. :thumbsup:

jonah: addressed, pushed. Tests green.

maya: Thanks both — merging now. :white_check_mark:
